usage: run_h2_contact.py [-h] --mode {probe,inspect,collect} [--model MODEL]
                         [--inventory INVENTORY] --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                         [--config CONFIG]
                         [--sensor-reference SENSOR_REFERENCE]
                         [--contact-probe CONTACT_PROBE]
                         [--sole-mode {original,tiled}] [--episodes EPISODES]
                         [--duration DURATION] [--headless] [--device DEVICE]

Convert/inspect H2, probe PhysX contact reporting, or collect tactile
trajectories. Run inside the user's EXISTING Isaac Lab environment; --help
needs only stdlib.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --mode {probe,inspect,collect}
  --model MODEL         Unmodified source MJCF; required for inspect/collect
  --inventory INVENTORY
                        Successful inspect_h2_model.py JSON for this MJCF
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                        NEW directory for USD, logs and records
  --config CONFIG
  --sensor-reference SENSOR_REFERENCE
  --contact-probe CONTACT_PROBE
                        Successful contact_probe.json; required for collect
  --sole-mode {original,tiled}
                        Override configured collision mode
  --episodes EPISODES   Override episode count
  --duration DURATION   Override seconds per episode
  --headless
  --device DEVICE       Physics device; start with cpu, then probe again for
                        cuda:0

usage: validate_h2_recording.py [-h] --run-dir RUN_DIR --output OUTPUT

Read a completed recording on any stdlib-only Python, without Isaac or NumPy.

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --run-dir RUN_DIR
  --output OUTPUT    NEW readback JSON
